## Context
The critical-name denylist in scripts/bash-env.sh (`_be_is_protected_name`) now
covers the high-severity RCE/hijack classes (GCONV_PATH, LD_*, interpreter
option vars, git/pager exec vectors). Gaze on PR #610 deferred two low-severity
tidy-ups.

## Actions
1. Extend `_be_is_protected_name` with the remaining low-severity vars a hostile
   project `.env` could set to perturb (not hijack) a child: PS0, TZ, TZDIR,
   LOCALDOMAIN, TERMINFO, LD_DEBUG, LD_PROFILE, BASH_XTRACEFD, HISTFILE. None is
   a code-exec vector; each is defence-in-depth.
2. Collapse any still-duplicated inline `GUARD_`/`_be_*` name checks at the two
   export sites into the single `_be_is_protected_name` predicate, so the
   denylist cannot drift between the parse path and the KEYS path.

## Test
- Extend tests/test_bash_env_keys_protect_critical_names.sh with the new names
  (assert each is refused on both the strict-parse and KEYS-selection paths).

## Exit criteria
- [x] New vars refused on both export paths, red-proven
- [x] Single predicate is the only name-policy site (no duplicated inline lists)
- [x] make check passes
